{
  "//": "Read-only Grafana MCP server for AI coding agents (Claude Code reads .mcp.json; Codex CLI uses its own ~/.codex config with the same command/env). It lets an agent query Loki (LogQL) and Prometheus (PromQL) and read dashboards through the already-public Grafana at metrics.example.com — so the internal Loki/Prometheus stay unexposed. SETUP: (1) In Grafana > Administration > Users and access > Service accounts, create a service account with the **Viewer** role only, then add a token. (2) Copy the `grafana` block into your real .mcp.json and set GRAFANA_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN from your shell/keychain (or Infisical) — do NOT commit it (.mcp.json is gitignored). (3) Requires Docker. `--disable-write` keeps the server read-only as defense-in-depth even if the token were ever over-scoped. See docs/audits/2026-06-16-ai-friendly-architecture-benchmark.md §3.1.",
  "mcpServers": {
    "grafana": {
      "command": "docker",
      "args": [
        "run",
        "--rm",
        "-i",
        "-e",
        "GRAFANA_URL=https://metrics.example.com",
        "-e",
        "GRAFANA_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN",
        "grafana/mcp-grafana",
        "-t",
        "stdio",
        "--disable-write"
      ],
      "env": {
        "GRAFANA_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN": "${GRAFANA_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN}"
      }
    }
  }
}
